---
description: Enforce semantic light and dark theme usage in Expo UI
globs: apps/mobile/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Expo themes

- Never hardcode UI colors in screens or components.
- Read semantic colors from `useTheme()` and type style factories with `ThemeColors`.
- Add new palette values to both light and dark themes with semantic names.
- Do not name tokens after visual values such as `gray500` or `purple`; use roles such as `textMuted`, `surface`, or `accent`.
- Keep the system color scheme as the default until a saved user preference exists.
- Persist manual theme changes and keep web/native behavior equivalent.
- Set status bar and native system background from the resolved theme.
- Check contrast, disabled, selected, error, success, and focus states in both themes.
